{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bmhxpzoym","tool_use_id":"toolu_0122z3hwurnEJAVQK7MScqpm","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run3-repo/9774e20d-457a-48d1-8caf-5f31346add3c/tasks/bmhxpzoym.output","summary":"Background command \"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; C=iter_1/candidate_5\ncat > $C/model_name.txt << 'EOF'\nsigned_commitment_heads_rigged_motif\nEOF\ncat > $C/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nRefinement of `attentive_lapse_heads_rigged_motif` (people judge a sequence random to the extent their own second-order model of a fair coin explains it better than the regular generators they suspect — a switch-biased coin, a heads-favoured trick coin and a repeating motif with slips — the evidence weighed per flip, with person-specific sensitivity and side habit, and a person-specific share of trials answered at random). The single change is that a person's departure from their own judgment is not capped at random guessing: each person's commitment to their randomness impression is drawn from a population that is mostly near full commitment but can fall below zero, so a few participants systematically pick the sequence that looks *less* random to everyone else (having reversed the question), agreeing with the majority well below chance — in the data four participants agree on only 22–41% of trials, which no lapse rate can produce — addressing the FDR-surviving critique that participants' agreement with the majority varies across people more than the lapse model produces.\nEOF\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc=open('models/attentive_lapse_heads_rigged_motif.py').read()\nhead='''\"\"\"Signed person-specific commitment on the heads-rigged second-order motif judgment.\n\nRefinement of `attentive_lapse_heads_rigged_motif` (described below). Single\nchange: the lapse lambda_i in [0, 1] (p_left = lambda_i/2 + (1-lambda_i) p_judged)\nis generalised to a signed commitment c_i in (-1, 1):\np_left = 1/2 + c_i (p_judged - 1/2), with c_i = 2 sigmoid(mu_c + sigma_c z_i) - 1\n(non-centred population, 400 slots, prior mass near full commitment). c_i >= 0\nis exactly the lapse model with lambda_i = 1 - c_i; c_i < 0 is a person who\nsystematically picks the sequence that looks less random (a reversed reading of\nthe question), so their agreement with the majority falls below chance, which\nno lapse rate can produce. Addresses the FDR-surviving critique that agreement\nwith the majority varies across people more than the lapse model produces.\n\nDescription of the refined model follows.\n\n'''\nbody=src.split('\"\"\"',1)[1]\nsrc=head+body\nold=src[src.index('    # Person-specific lapse rate'):src.index('    chose_left = pm.Data')]\nnew='''    # Person-specific signed commitment to the judgment: near 1 for most\n    # people, 0 for a pure guesser, negative for a reversed responder.\n    mu_c = pm.Normal(\"mu_c\", mu=3.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_c = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_c\", sigma=1.5)\n    z_c = pm.Normal(\"z_c\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    commit = 2.0 * pm.math.sigmoid(mu_c + sigma_c * z_c)[pid] - 1.0\n\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\", pt.clip(0.5 + commit * (p_judged - 0.5), 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    )\n\n'''\nsrc=src.replace(old,new)\nopen('iter_1/candidate_5/candidate.py','w').write(src)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"lapse\\|commit\" $C/candidate.py | head -30\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_5 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"5cdf1ff1-4df0-4079-b71a-211c